{:title "What amu actually optimizes per ISA and hardware unit"
 :description
 "What amu emits and tunes today per ISA and hardware unit, with gates attached. Measured vs mechanism-only vs HOLD. No invented speedups. No Kotoba-beats-Rust-or-C on GPU."
 :eyebrow "Compiler / hardware"
 :intro
 "This note is for someone who needs to know what amu emits and tunes today, with gates attached, so they can decide whether a measured path helps their workload. Kotoba Labs Inc operates the public surface at https://kotoba-lang.org. The working philosophy is 他者の達成を助ける: help someone else finish one more piece of work. Every claim below is marked in prose as measured, mechanism-only, HOLD/unknown, or not-applicable. Presence of a compiler knob is not a wall-clock win. No invented speedups, percentages, FLOPS, or GMV appear here. There is no claim that Kotoba beats Rust or C on Cerebras, NVIDIA, or AMD."
 :notice
 "Draft for review 2026-09-10. Evidence-led. Philosophy: help someone else finish one more piece of work (他者の達成を助ける). English-primary; translated bodies were not invented."
 :sections
 [{:title "What amu emits today"
   :paragraphs
   ["Pipeline (README + CHANGELOG, mechanism-only): source → inert reader → typed/effect HIR → SSA-like KIR → backend → independent verifier → admission."
    "Emit families (mechanism-only unless noted):"]
   :items
   ["Wasm32: wasm32, wasm32-browser, wasm32-wasi → sealed :wasm32-*-kotoba-v1"
    "x86_64 KEXE: x86_64, x86_64-linux, x86_64-macos, x86_64-windows → sealed :kexe/v1"
    "AArch64 KEXE: aarch64, aarch64-linux, aarch64-macos, aarch64-windows, aarch64-android, aarch64-ios"
    "aiueos freestanding: x86_64-aiueos-{uefi,kernel,user}-v1, aarch64-aiueos-kernel-v1 (ELF64/PE32+)"
    "CLJS / JS / EVM: --target cljs, restricted js, --target evm (:evm256-kotoba-v1)"
    "GPU accelerator KIR: :kotoba.accelerator-kir/v1 → sealed :kotoba.gpu-artifact/v1 as WGSL / CUDA C / MSL source text (:wgsl-v1 :cuda-v1 :msl-v1) — not a product GPU runtime"]
   :after
   "ADR 0001: ISA emission alone is not platform support. GPUs/NPUs planned as bounded accelerator effects. Product GPU/NPU support HOLD/unknown. JDK-free emit: bin/amu compile/check for wasm32* and ordinary x86_64*/aarch64* can run under nbb. Selected IR pins: word/f64/kernel-memory/runtime-call (ADR 0240–0244); f32 on both native ISAs through six gates (ADR 0292)."}
  {:title "CPU microarch knobs that actually exist"
   :paragraphs
   ["Mechanism-only unless noted. A compiler knob is not a wall-clock win."]
   :rows
   [["AArch64 logical-seeded constants (ADR 0278)"
     "mechanism-only plus size measured. ORR-immediate seed + MOVK when shorter; ≤8 recognizer probes; x86 unchanged. Size measured; timing discarded."]
